34 0 obj
<< /Length 3073 >>
stream
BT /F2 8 Tf 54.00 814.00 Td (Complete Report and Interview Q&A) Tj ET
BT /F1 8 Tf 532.20 24.00 Td (16) Tj ET
BT /F2 11 Tf 54.00 772.00 Td (10. What is LTspice used for in this project?) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54.00 748.00 Td (LTspice is used to simulate rail startup timing and the Rail C load transient.) Tj ET
BT /F2 11 Tf 54.00 725.00 Td (11. What is KiCad used for in this project?) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54.00 701.00 Td (KiCad is used to create the schematic, assign symbols, export a netlist/BOM/PDF, and run) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54.00 687.00 Td (electrical rule checking.) Tj ET
BT /F2 11 Tf 54.00 664.00 Td (12. What does ERC mean?) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54.00 640.00 Td (ERC means Electrical Rules Check. It checks schematic-level electrical issues such as) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54.00 626.00 Td (unconnected pins, conflicting pin types, and other schematic problems.) Tj ET
BT /F2 11 Tf 54.00 603.00 Td (13. Did the KiCad schematic pass ERC?) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54.00 579.00 Td (Yes. The exported ERC report shows 0 errors and 0 warnings.) Tj ET
BT /F2 11 Tf 54.00 556.00 Td (14. What is a regulator?) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54.00 532.00 Td (A regulator converts an input voltage into a stable output voltage.) Tj ET
BT /F2 11 Tf 54.00 509.00 Td (15. What is an LDO?) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54.00 485.00 Td (An LDO is a low-dropout linear regulator. It is simple and low-noise, but it can waste) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54.00 471.00 Td (power as heat.) Tj ET
BT /F2 11 Tf 54.00 448.00 Td (16. What is a buck converter?) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54.00 424.00 Td (A buck converter is a switching regulator that efficiently steps a higher voltage down) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54.00 410.00 Td (to a lower voltage.) Tj ET
BT /F2 11 Tf 54.00 387.00 Td (17. Why use capacitors on the outputs?) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54.00 363.00 Td (Output capacitors reduce ripple and help supply current during fast load changes.) Tj ET
BT /F2 11 Tf 54.00 340.00 Td (18. What is a test point?) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54.00 316.00 Td (A test point is a probe-accessible node used during measurement and debugging.) Tj ET
BT /F2 11 Tf 54.00 293.00 Td (19. What is the project's strongest point?) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54.00 269.00 Td (The strongest point is that it shows a complete workflow: requirements, simulation,) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54.00 255.00 Td (schematic, validation reports, BOM, documentation, and interview explanation.) Tj ET
BT /F2 11 Tf 54.00 232.00 Td (20. What is the simplest way to explain the project?) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54.00 208.00 Td (It is a 5 V input power board that creates three controlled rails for an embedded system) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54.00 194.00 Td (and verifies their startup order in LTspice.) Tj ET
BT /F2 14 Tf 54.00 163.00 Td (Intermediate Level: Design Choices) Tj ET
BT /F2 11 Tf 54.00 134.00 Td (21. Why are multiple rails needed in an SoC system?) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54.00 110.00 Td (Different sections of an SoC need different voltages. Core logic often needs a low) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54.00 96.00 Td (voltage like 1.2 V, I/O may need 1.8 V, and external sensors often need 3.3 V.) Tj ET
endstream
endobj
35 0 obj
<< /Type /Page /Parent 54 0 R /MediaBox [0 0 595 842] /Resources << /Font << /F1 1 0 R /F2 2 0 R /F3 3 0 R >> >> /Contents 34 0 R >>
