38 0 obj
<< /Length 3069 >>
stream
BT /F2 8 Tf 54.00 814.00 Td (Complete Report and Interview Q&A) Tj ET
BT /F1 8 Tf 532.20 24.00 Td (18) Tj ET
BT /F2 11 Tf 54.00 772.00 Td (35. What does the 22 uF output capacitor do?) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54.00 748.00 Td (It provides local charge, reduces ripple, and helps reduce voltage droop during) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54.00 734.00 Td (transient events.) Tj ET
BT /F2 11 Tf 54.00 711.00 Td (36. Why use X7R ceramic capacitors?) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54.00 687.00 Td (X7R capacitors have better temperature stability than lower-grade dielectrics and are) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54.00 673.00 Td (common for decoupling.) Tj ET
BT /F2 11 Tf 54.00 650.00 Td (37. What is ESR?) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54.00 626.00 Td (ESR is equivalent series resistance. It is the effective resistance inside a capacitor) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54.00 612.00 Td (and affects ripple and transient voltage drop.) Tj ET
BT /F2 11 Tf 54.00 589.00 Td (38. What is ESL?) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54.00 565.00 Td (ESL is equivalent series inductance. It limits how well a capacitor responds at very) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54.00 551.00 Td (high frequencies.) Tj ET
BT /F2 11 Tf 54.00 528.00 Td (39. Why place capacitors near regulator pins?) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54.00 504.00 Td (Short placement reduces parasitic inductance and resistance, improving transient) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54.00 490.00 Td (response and reducing noise.) Tj ET
BT /F2 11 Tf 54.00 467.00 Td (40. Why include reverse-polarity protection?) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54.00 443.00 Td (It protects the board if the input supply is connected backwards.) Tj ET
BT /F2 11 Tf 54.00 420.00 Td (41. What is the downside of a Schottky diode for input protection?) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54.00 396.00 Td (It has a forward voltage drop and dissipates heat.) Tj ET
BT /F2 11 Tf 54.00 373.00 Td (42. What is a better production reverse-protection method?) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54.00 349.00 Td (A P-MOSFET ideal-diode style circuit or ideal diode controller gives lower voltage drop) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54.00 335.00 Td (and better efficiency.) Tj ET
BT /F2 11 Tf 54.00 312.00 Td (43. Why include a P-MOSFET load switch?) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54.00 288.00 Td (It allows the sensor rail to be disconnected, sequenced, or power-gated.) Tj ET
BT /F2 11 Tf 54.00 265.00 Td (44. What does an enable pin do?) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54.00 241.00 Td (An enable pin turns a regulator on or off.) Tj ET
BT /F2 11 Tf 54.00 218.00 Td (45. How can an RC delay create sequencing?) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54.00 194.00 Td (A resistor charges a capacitor. The regulator enable pin turns on when the capacitor) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54.00 180.00 Td (voltage crosses its threshold.) Tj ET
BT /F2 11 Tf 54.00 157.00 Td (46. What is the approximate RC delay formula?) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54.00 133.00 Td (For a charging capacitor, `t = -RC ln\(1 - Vth/Vin\)`.) Tj ET
BT /F2 11 Tf 54.00 110.00 Td (47. Why are RC delays not exact?) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54.00 86.00 Td (They vary with resistor tolerance, capacitor tolerance, leakage, temperature, and enable) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54.00 72.00 Td (threshold variation.) Tj ET
endstream
endobj
39 0 obj
<< /Type /Page /Parent 54 0 R /MediaBox [0 0 595 842] /Resources << /Font << /F1 1 0 R /F2 2 0 R /F3 3 0 R >> >> /Contents 38 0 R >>
endobj
40 0 obj
<< /Length 3016 >>
stream
BT /F2 8 Tf 54.00 814.00 Td (Complete Report and Interview Q&A) Tj ET
BT /F1 8 Tf 532.20 24.00 Td (19) Tj ET
BT /F2 11 Tf 54.00 772.00 Td (48. What is better than RC sequencing for production?) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54.00 748.00 Td (A power sequencer IC, supervisor, PMIC, or microcontroller-controlled enable sequence is) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54.00 734.00 Td (more precise.) Tj ET
BT /F2 11 Tf 54.00 711.00 Td (49. Why include test points on enable nets?) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54.00 687.00 Td (Enable test points let me verify that the sequence is actually happening at the) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54.00 673.00 Td (regulator control pins.) Tj ET
BT /F2 11 Tf 54.00 650.00 Td (50. Why include test points on every rail?) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54.00 626.00 Td (They make bring-up and debugging easier because every important voltage can be probed) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54.00 612.00 Td (directly.) Tj ET
BT /F2 14 Tf 54.00 581.00 Td (Intermediate Level: LTspice And Simulation) Tj ET
BT /F2 11 Tf 54.00 552.00 Td (51. Why use behavioral sources in LTspice?) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54.00 528.00 Td (Behavioral sources make the architecture easy to simulate without getting blocked by) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54.00 514.00 Td (fragile vendor model setup.) Tj ET
BT /F2 11 Tf 54.00 491.00 Td (52. Does the behavioral simulation model real switching ripple?) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54.00 467.00 Td (No. It models startup timing and load behavior, but not actual buck switching ripple or) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54.00 453.00 Td (compensation loop details.) Tj ET
BT /F2 11 Tf 54.00 430.00 Td (53. Why is that acceptable for this stage?) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54.00 406.00 Td (At the architecture stage, the main goal is to verify sequencing and load response) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54.00 392.00 Td (conceptually. Detailed regulator simulation can come later.) Tj ET
BT /F2 11 Tf 54.00 369.00 Td (54. What does `.tran 20m startup` do?) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54.00 345.00 Td (It runs a transient simulation for 20 ms and starts from initial startup conditions.) Tj ET
BT /F2 11 Tf 54.00 322.00 Td (55. What signals should be plotted?) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54.00 298.00 Td (Plot the three rail voltages and the three enable signals: `V\(RAIL_A_1V2\)`,) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54.00 284.00 Td (`V\(RAIL_B_1V8\)`, `V\(RAIL_C_3V3\)`, `V\(EN_A\)`, `V\(EN_B\)`, and `V\(EN_C\)`.) Tj ET
BT /F2 11 Tf 54.00 261.00 Td (56. What do the `.meas` commands do?) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54.00 237.00 Td (They automatically measure rail startup times and Rail C voltage behavior) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54.00 223.00 Td (before/during/after the load step.) Tj ET
BT /F2 11 Tf 54.00 200.00 Td (57. Why measure 90% rail time?) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54.00 176.00 Td (90% of nominal is a common practical threshold for determining when a rail is mostly up.) Tj ET
BT /F2 11 Tf 54.00 153.00 Td (58. What is 90% of 1.2 V?) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54.00 129.00 Td (`0.9 * 1.2 = 1.08 V`.) Tj ET
BT /F2 11 Tf 54.00 106.00 Td (59. What is 90% of 1.8 V?) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54.00 82.00 Td (`0.9 * 1.8 = 1.62 V`.) Tj ET
endstream
endobj
41 0 obj
<< /Type /Page /Parent 54 0 R /MediaBox [0 0 595 842] /Resources << /Font << /F1 1 0 R /F2 2 0 R /F3 3 0 R >> >> /Contents 40 0 R >>
endobj
42 0 obj
<< /Length 3237 >>
stream
BT /F2 8 Tf 54.00 814.00 Td (Complete Report and Interview Q&A) Tj ET
BT /F1 8 Tf 532.20 24.00 Td (20) Tj ET
BT /F2 11 Tf 54.00 772.00 Td (60. What is 90% of 3.3 V?) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54.00 748.00 Td (`0.9 * 3.3 = 2.97 V`.) Tj ET
BT /F2 11 Tf 54.00 725.00 Td (61. Why did you move long formulas into `.func` directives?) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54.00 701.00 Td (To keep the LTspice schematic visually clean. The source values stay short, while the) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54.00 687.00 Td (detailed equations live in a directive block.) Tj ET
BT /F2 11 Tf 54.00 664.00 Td (62. What is the purpose of `V=RA\(time\)`?) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54.00 640.00 Td (It tells the behavioral source to output the Rail A voltage according to the `RA\(t\)`) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54.00 626.00 Td (function.) Tj ET
BT /F2 11 Tf 54.00 603.00 Td (63. Why are enable signals included as separate sources?) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54.00 579.00 Td (They make the intended sequence visible in the waveform plot.) Tj ET
BT /F2 11 Tf 54.00 556.00 Td (64. How would you improve the simulation for production?) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54.00 532.00 Td (Use verified manufacturer models, include inductors and feedback components, model input) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54.00 518.00 Td (supply ramp, include ESR/ESL, and run corner cases.) Tj ET
BT /F2 11 Tf 54.00 495.00 Td (65. What corner cases would you simulate?) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54.00 471.00 Td (Minimum/maximum input voltage, light/full load, startup into load, output short) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54.00 457.00 Td (behavior, temperature extremes, capacitor tolerance, and sequencing tolerance.) Tj ET
BT /F2 14 Tf 54.00 426.00 Td (Advanced Level: Regulator And Power Electronics) Tj ET
BT /F2 11 Tf 54.00 397.00 Td (66. Why might an LDO from 5 V to 1.2 V be thermally bad?) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54.00 373.00 Td (The power loss is `\(5 - 1.2\) * 0.5 = 1.9 W`, which is too high for many small packages.) Tj ET
BT /F2 11 Tf 54.00 350.00 Td (67. What would you use instead for high-current 1.2 V?) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54.00 326.00 Td (I would use a buck converter, possibly followed by a low-noise LDO if the rail needs) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54.00 312.00 Td (extra filtering.) Tj ET
BT /F2 11 Tf 54.00 289.00 Td (68. What is buck converter efficiency?) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54.00 265.00 Td (Efficiency is output power divided by input power. A buck converter is usually much more) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54.00 251.00 Td (efficient than an LDO for high voltage drop and high current.) Tj ET
BT /F2 11 Tf 54.00 228.00 Td (69. What is the purpose of the inductor in a buck converter?) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54.00 204.00 Td (The inductor stores and releases energy each switching cycle, smoothing current and) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54.00 190.00 Td (enabling efficient voltage conversion.) Tj ET
BT /F2 11 Tf 54.00 167.00 Td (70. What happens if the inductor is too small?) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54.00 143.00 Td (Ripple current increases, which can increase ripple, losses, current stress, and) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54.00 129.00 Td (possibly instability.) Tj ET
BT /F2 11 Tf 54.00 106.00 Td (71. What happens if the inductor is too large?) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54.00 82.00 Td (Transient response can become slower, size and cost increase, and the regulator may not) Tj ET
endstream
endobj
