44 0 obj
<< /Length 3002 >>
stream
BT /F2 8 Tf 54.00 814.00 Td (Complete Report and Interview Q&A) Tj ET
BT /F1 8 Tf 532.20 24.00 Td (21) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54.00 772.00 Td (operate optimally.) Tj ET
BT /F2 11 Tf 54.00 749.00 Td (72. What is switch-node ringing?) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54.00 725.00 Td (It is high-frequency oscillation at the switching node caused by parasitic inductance) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54.00 711.00 Td (and capacitance.) Tj ET
BT /F2 11 Tf 54.00 688.00 Td (73. Why is the switch node noisy?) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54.00 664.00 Td (It has fast voltage transitions and high di/dt current loops.) Tj ET
BT /F2 11 Tf 54.00 641.00 Td (74. How do you reduce switch-node noise?) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54.00 617.00 Td (Keep the switch node copper small, minimize loop area, use good grounding, and follow) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54.00 603.00 Td (datasheet layout recommendations.) Tj ET
BT /F2 11 Tf 54.00 580.00 Td (75. What is loop compensation?) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54.00 556.00 Td (Loop compensation shapes the regulator feedback loop so the output remains stable over) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54.00 542.00 Td (load, capacitor, and input conditions.) Tj ET
BT /F2 11 Tf 54.00 519.00 Td (76. What affects regulator stability?) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54.00 495.00 Td (Output capacitor value, ESR, inductor value, feedback network, load range, internal) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54.00 481.00 Td (compensation, and layout parasitics.) Tj ET
BT /F2 11 Tf 54.00 458.00 Td (77. What is load regulation?) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54.00 434.00 Td (Load regulation describes how much output voltage changes as load current changes.) Tj ET
BT /F2 11 Tf 54.00 411.00 Td (78. What is line regulation?) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54.00 387.00 Td (Line regulation describes how much output voltage changes as input voltage changes.) Tj ET
BT /F2 11 Tf 54.00 364.00 Td (79. What is dropout voltage?) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54.00 340.00 Td (Dropout voltage is the minimum voltage difference required between input and output for) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54.00 326.00 Td (an LDO to regulate correctly.) Tj ET
BT /F2 11 Tf 54.00 303.00 Td (80. What is quiescent current?) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54.00 279.00 Td (Quiescent current is the current consumed by the regulator itself to operate.) Tj ET
BT /F2 11 Tf 54.00 256.00 Td (81. What is soft-start?) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54.00 232.00 Td (Soft-start controls how quickly a regulator output rises, reducing inrush current and) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54.00 218.00 Td (overshoot.) Tj ET
BT /F2 11 Tf 54.00 195.00 Td (82. Why does startup inrush matter?) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54.00 171.00 Td (Large inrush current can trip the supply, stress components, or pull down other rails.) Tj ET
BT /F2 11 Tf 54.00 148.00 Td (83. What is output ripple?) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54.00 124.00 Td (Output ripple is AC variation on top of the DC output voltage.) Tj ET
BT /F2 11 Tf 54.00 101.00 Td (84. How would you measure ripple correctly?) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54.00 77.00 Td (Use an oscilloscope with short ground spring or coax method, proper bandwidth limit if) Tj ET
endstream
endobj
45 0 obj
<< /Type /Page /Parent 54 0 R /MediaBox [0 0 595 842] /Resources << /Font << /F1 1 0 R /F2 2 0 R /F3 3 0 R >> >> /Contents 44 0 R >>
