stream
BT /F2 8 Tf 54.00 814.00 Td (Complete Report and Interview Q&A) Tj ET
BT /F1 8 Tf 532.20 24.00 Td (24) Tj ET
BT /F2 11 Tf 54.00 772.00 Td (107. How do you estimate LDO junction temperature?) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54.00 748.00 Td (Calculate power loss, multiply by thermal resistance, and add ambient temperature: `Tj =) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54.00 734.00 Td (Ta + P * thetaJA`.) Tj ET
BT /F2 11 Tf 54.00 711.00 Td (108. How would you validate sequencing on hardware?) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54.00 687.00 Td (Use an oscilloscope to probe all enable pins and output rails at test points during) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54.00 673.00 Td (power-up and power-down.) Tj ET
BT /F2 11 Tf 54.00 650.00 Td (109. How would you validate load transient?) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54.00 626.00 Td (Use an electronic load to step current and capture voltage droop and recovery on the) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54.00 612.00 Td (oscilloscope.) Tj ET
BT /F2 11 Tf 54.00 589.00 Td (110. What would you check if Rail B starts before Rail A is stable?) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54.00 565.00 Td (Check the enable timing circuit, RC values, enable thresholds, power-good signals, and) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54.00 551.00 Td (input ramp behavior.) Tj ET
BT /F2 11 Tf 54.00 528.00 Td (111. What would you check if Rail C droops too much?) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54.00 504.00 Td (Check output capacitance, capacitor ESR/ESL, regulator transient response, layout, load) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54.00 490.00 Td (step magnitude, and current limit.) Tj ET
BT /F2 11 Tf 54.00 467.00 Td (112. What would you check if a rail oscillates?) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54.00 443.00 Td (Check regulator stability, output capacitor value/ESR, feedback routing, layout, and) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54.00 429.00 Td (datasheet compensation guidance.) Tj ET
BT /F2 11 Tf 54.00 406.00 Td (113. What layout issue can break a buck converter?) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54.00 382.00 Td (Large high-current loop area or poor switch-node layout can create noise, ringing, EMI,) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54.00 368.00 Td (and instability.) Tj ET
BT /F2 11 Tf 54.00 345.00 Td (114. Why is a ground plane important?) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54.00 321.00 Td (A ground plane provides low-impedance return paths, reduces noise, and improves thermal) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54.00 307.00 Td (spreading.) Tj ET
BT /F2 11 Tf 54.00 284.00 Td (115. How would you handle analog sensors on the 3.3 V rail?) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54.00 260.00 Td (I might add filtering, local decoupling, ferrite bead isolation, or a low-noise LDO if) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54.00 246.00 Td (the sensor is noise-sensitive.) Tj ET
BT /F2 11 Tf 54.00 223.00 Td (116. What is the difference between schematic correctness and layout) Tj ET
BT /F2 11 Tf 54.00 208.00 Td (correctness?) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54.00 184.00 Td (Schematic correctness means the logical circuit connections are right. Layout) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54.00 170.00 Td (correctness means physical placement, routing, grounding, thermal, and noise behavior) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54.00 156.00 Td (are right.) Tj ET
BT /F2 11 Tf 54.00 133.00 Td (117. Why include both `.asc` and `.cir` files?) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54.00 109.00 Td (The `.asc` is easier to view and edit visually. The `.cir` is a plain-text companion) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54.00 95.00 Td (netlist useful for review and fallback simulation.) Tj ET
endstream
